* `.temp` gate (2.52.0): resistor_noise_va.net at 100 degC instead of 27 degC.
* The same two compiled resistors (models/resistor.va, whose noise is
*   I(p,n) <+ white_noise(4*`P_K*$temperature/R)
* ) across a 1 V source, probed at their junction. `.temp 100` builds the models at 373.15 K, so
* `$temperature` reads it and the spectrum is 4kT*(R1||R2) at 373.15 K:
*   S(out) = 4 * 1.380649e-23 * 373.15 * 750 ~ 1.546e-17 V^2/Hz, flat,
* i.e. resistor_noise_va.net's answer times 373.15/300.15. Pure R/V, so QSPICE runs it as written,
* with its own resistors at its own `.temp`.
*   cargo run -p va-cli -- sim circuits/resistor_noise_hot.net --model models/resistor.va --noise
V1 in  gnd  DC 1
R1 in  a    1000
R2 a   gnd  3000
.temp 100
.noise V(a) V1 dec 10 10 10meg
.end
